      ":question/problem": "$$\n(x-1){y}^{\u2033}+{y}^{\u2032}+\\frac{1}{(x-1)^{2}}y=0\n$$\n\nConsider the differential equation given above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The functions $P(x)=\\frac{1}{x-1}$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{1}{(x-1)^{3}}$ are analytic about $x=1.$\n- The functions $(x-1)P(x)$ and $(x-1)^{2}Q(x)$ are analytic about $x=1.$\n- The point $x=1$ is an **irregular** singular point of the differential equation."
